PUBLIC RESPONSE: The gene to knock out is phdA (encoding the CoA ligase that activates p-coumarate as the first step of its catabolic pathway in C. glutamicum). This blocks entry into the subsequent β-oxidative degradation route without affecting the introduced biosynthetic pathway for p-coumaric acid production.

(The answer is based on the known phdABCD operon responsible for phenylpropanoid catabolism in this organism; other candidates such as pobA act downstream after conversion to 4-hydroxybenzoate and are therefore less direct.)

}

